1 | fields | The fields west of Spangler's Spring exposed Confederate troops to fire from 28 Union guns on the third day; 6 acres of trees to be removed to reopen them (2009) | - | 1863-07-03 (the fields that exposed the Confederate troops; the tree removal is a modern work) | stated | The newsletter says the goal of removing six acres of nonhistoric trees was to re-open the fields that exposed Confederate troops in and around the Spangler's Spring area to heavy fire from 28 Union guns, 18 of them on and around Powers' Hill, in the engagement of July 3, 1863 | =Six acres of trees will be removed, provided soil conditions are dry enough or cold enough this fall and winter. The goal is to re-open the fields that exposed Confederate troops in and around the Spangler's Spring area to heavy fire from 28 Union guns - 18 of them concentrated on and around Powers' Hill alone. Confederate regiments engaged the Union positions here on the far right flank of the Union line during a seven hour engagement on July 3, 1863, that started before dawn. ~R
