2 | orchards | In 1863 almost every farm of any size had orchards; troops took cover in them, they concealed movement and people gathered in them to rest or seek medical assistance | - | 1863-07 | stated | The newsletter says that in 1863 almost every farm of any size in Gettysburg had orchards, in which troops took cover, which could conceal movement and where people gathered to rest or seek medical assistance | =In 1863, almost every farm of any size in Gettysburg had orchards. The orchards played many roles during the battle: troops took cover in them; they could be used to conceal movement; and they were places to gather to rest or seek medical assistance. ~R
