2 | fences | Fences replaced in the summer of 2012: Sherfy hog fence, Slyder lane post and board fence, Emmitsburg Road hog fence, Spangler farm post and board fence, picket fences at the Hummelbaugh, Rose, Bushman, Spangler, Klingel, Trostle and Althoff farms | bld-sherfy-farm,bld-slyder-farm,bld-hummelbaugh-farm,bld-rose-farm,bld-bushman-farm,bld-klingle-farm,bld-trostle-farm | ~2012 (fences replaced that summer; a modern reconstruction) | stated | The newsletter says that in the summer the park replaced numerous historic fences, among them the Sherfy hog fence, the Slyder lane post and board fence, the Emmitsburg Road hog fence, the Spangler farm's post and board fence and the picket fences at the Hummelbaugh, Rose, Bushman, Spangler, Klingel, Trostle and Althoff farms | =This summer we replaced numerous historic fences on the battlefield, including: the Sherfy hog fence, the Slyder lane post and board fence, the Emmitsburg Road hog fence, the Spangler farm's post and board fence, and the picket fences at the Hummelbaugh, Rose, Bushman, Spangler, Klingel, Trostle and Althoff farms. ~R
2 | fences | Fences reconstructed in 2012: stone and rider fences behind the U.S. Regulars monument, from the Trostle farm to Wheatfield Road and along Wheatfield Road by the Althoff house; Virginia worm fence from the U.S. Regulars monument to the Codori farm; post and rail at the Weikert house | bld-trostle-farm,bld-codori-farm,bld-weikert-farm | ~2012 (fences reconstructed that summer; a modern reconstruction) | stated | The newsletter says park staff also reconstructed the stone and rider fence behind the U.S. Regulars monument, the stone and rider fence from the Trostle farm to Wheatfield Road, a section of Virginia worm fence from the U.S. Regulars monument to the Codori farm, the stone and rider fence along Wheatfield Road by the Althoff house and a post and rail fence at the Weikert house | =Park staff also reconstructed the stone and rider fence behind the U.S. Regulars monument; the stone and rider fence that runs from the Trostle farm to Wheatfield Road; a section of Virginia Worm fence that runs from U.S. Regulars monument to the Codori farm; the stone and rider fence along Wheatfield Rd. by the Althoff house; and a post and rail fence at the Weikert house. ~R
2 | fences | Fences rebuilt in 2012 at Culp's pasture (post and rail), Benner's Hill (post and rail) and along the Chambersburg Pike (new Virginia worm on the east side, post and rail on the west side) | - | ~2012 (fences built that summer; a modern reconstruction) | stated | The newsletter says the team completely reconstructed the post and rail fence on the west side of Culp's pasture and the post and rail fence at Benner's Hill along the property line, and with volunteers built new Virginia worm fence along the east side of the Chambersburg Pike from Lee's Headquarters north to Plum Run and new post and rail on the west side of the pike | =The team completely re-constructed the post and rail fence on the west side of Culp's pasture by the Slocum equestrian monument and the post and rail fence at Benner's Hill along the property line. In addition, together with Friends of Gettysburg volunteers we built new Virginia worm along the east side Chambersburg Pike from Lee's Headquarters north to Plum Run, and new post and rail on the west side of Chambersburg Pike. ~R
